---
description: Core behavioral guidelines for all AI work in this NestJS project
alwaysApply: true
---

- Think before coding - state assumptions, surface tradeoffs, and ask when ambiguity blocks progress.
- Simplicity first - write the minimum code that solves the request and avoid speculative abstractions.
- Surgical changes - touch only what serves the request and clean up only what your change makes unused.
- Goal-driven execution - define short steps with verification checks and loop until the result is proven.
- House rules - no em dashes, read relevant conventions first, write summaries to `do-work/summaries/`, and use Conventional Commits.
- Toolchain - yarn via corepack. Verify with `yarn tsc --noEmit`, `yarn lint`, `yarn test`, `yarn build`.
